      "strengths_deep_dive": [
        "MAS-GLA focuses heavily on youth empowerment through its <cite id=\"7\">Tarbiya and Youth Ministry programs</cite>. These initiatives are designed to move people toward God-consciousness and justice. The organization\u2019s ability to scale is evident in its <cite id=\"8\">32,000 beneficiaries</cite>, achieved with a lean financial model. Its <cite id=\"6\">77.3% program expense ratio</cite> in FY2024 filings suggests a highly direct application of donor funds to these community services."
      ],
      "summary": "The Muslim American Society of Greater Los Angeles (MAS-GLA) operates as a community-focused organization dedicated to youth development and religious education. Founded in <cite id=\"1\">1993</cite>, the organization has spent over three decades providing <cite id=\"2\">direct services to the community</cite>. In FY2024, the charity reported <cite id=\"3\">total revenue of $1,168,118</cite>, reflecting a significant <cite id=\"4\">3-year revenue growth rate of 30.5%</cite>. The organization maintains a high level of financial efficiency in its fundraising efforts. It spends only <cite id=\"5\">$0.03 to raise every $1</cite> in donations. While the organization is not fully rated by major agencies, it reports a <cite id=\"6\">program expense ratio of 77.3%</cite> in its most recent filings. This indicates that all reported expenses are directed toward its core mission of <cite id=\"7\">youth ministry and Tarbiya programs</cite>. The charity serves a substantial population, with data indicating <cite id=\"8\">32,000 beneficiaries served</cite> through its various leadership and social justice initiatives. As a <cite id=\"9\">zakat-eligible organization</cite>, it provides a verified pathway for Muslim donors to fulfill their religious obligations through programs that support <cite id=\"10\">fisabilillah (in the way of God)</cite> categories.",
